 "title": "ZnS QDs and CdS QDs Toxicity in Yeast Strains",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the toxicity of ZnS QDs and CdS QDs in yeast strains. S. cerevisiae, a yeast organism, is exposed to ZnS QDs and ZnSO4, leading to the induction of ROS, which in turn causes ZnS QDs to be hypersensitive to pos5Δ. CdS QDs are also exposed to YKO collections, a type of yeast strain, and have a higher tolerance to glr1Δ. The study uses various methods, including sequencing, dynamic light scattering, and DAVID, to analyze the effects of these nanomaterials on yeast cells and their mitochondria.",
